# EtUserInfo Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtUserInfo` is a compound UI component for rendering a user identity block with:

- Avatar (always square for users)
- Primary text (`Title`)
- Secondary text (`Subtitle`)

It supports two layouts:

- `horizontal`: avatar on the left, title/subtitle stacked on the right
- `vertical`: avatar, then title, then subtitle in a column

This component is intentionally presentational. It does not manage fetching, navigation, selection state, or business logic.

## Relationship to EtUserProfileHeader.UserInfo

`EtUserProfileHeader.UserInfo` (in `layout/headers/user-profile/subcomponents/user-info.tsx`) is a **different component**:

- **EtUserProfileHeader.UserInfo**: Context-driven, part of the user profile header layout. Consumes `UserProfileContext`, slots: Avatar, Name, UserName, Copiers. Use only within `<EtUserProfileHeader>`.
- **EtUserInfo**: Data-driven, standalone data display. Accepts `EtUserData` prop, slots: Avatar, Title, Subtitle. Use for user identity blocks anywhere (lists, cards, etc.).

For new user identity blocks outside the profile header, prefer `EtUserInfo`.

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtUserInfo` (main component)

```tsx
<EtUserInfo
  data={{
    avatar?: {
      source: string,                  // required when using EtUserInfo.Avatar
      size?: 'small' | 'medium' | 'large', // default: 'medium'
      alt?: string,
    },
    title?: string,                         // used when Title has no children
    subtitle?: string,                     // used when Subtitle has no children
  }}
  layout?: 'horizontal' | 'vertical'       // default: 'horizontal'
  ellipsizeMode?: 'head' | 'middle' | 'tail' | 'clip'  // default: 'tail'
  maxWidth?: number                        // horizontal layout only; constrains text block
  shrink?: boolean                         // default: false — horizontal layout only; lets the text block shrink beside fixed-width siblings
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
>
  {children}
</EtUserInfo>
```

- `layout`, `ellipsizeMode`, `maxWidth`, and `shrink` are **root-level props**.
- `data.title` and `data.subtitle` are optional; when set, `<EtUserInfo.Title />` and `<EtUserInfo.Subtitle />` can be used with no children to render that text.
- User avatars are always square (shapeOverride); `data.avatar.shape` is ignored.

`children` are expected to be compound subcomponents:

- `<EtUserInfo.Avatar />`
- `<EtUserInfo.Title>...</EtUserInfo.Title>`
- `<EtUserInfo.Subtitle>...</EtUserInfo.Subtitle>`

### `EtUserInfo.Avatar`

```tsx
<EtUserInfo.Avatar style={avatarStyle}>
  {/* optional EtAvatar.Badge / overlays */}
</EtUserInfo.Avatar>
```

- Reads `avatar` config from context (no direct avatar props).
- Renders `null` when `avatar.source` is missing/empty.
- Always renders square avatar (shapeOverride).
- Forwards `children` into `InfoAvatar` / `EtAvatar` (e.g. trader crown via `EtAvatar.Badge`).

### `shrink`

When the row sits next to siblings that must keep their intrinsic width (e.g. rates on a card footer), pass `shrink`:

```tsx
<EtUserInfo data={user} shrink>
  <EtUserInfo.Avatar />
  <EtUserInfo.Title />
  <EtUserInfo.Subtitle />
</EtUserInfo>
```

### `EtUserInfo.Title`

```tsx
<EtUserInfo.Title>{ReactNode}</EtUserInfo.Title>
```

- Delegates to internal `InfoText` with `value={data.title}`, `variant="label-primary-semibold"`, and theme color.
- **No children and no `data.title`**: renders `null`.
- **No children but `data.title` is set**: renders `EtText` with `data.title`, `numberOfLines={1}`, and `ellipsizeMode` from context.
- **Has children**: renders a horizontal row wrapper for custom composition.

### `EtUserInfo.Subtitle`

```tsx
<EtUserInfo.Subtitle>{ReactNode}</EtUserInfo.Subtitle>
```

- Delegates to internal `InfoText` with `value={data.subtitle}` and `variant="label-tertiary-regular"`.
- **No children and no `data.subtitle`**: renders `null`.
- **No children but `data.subtitle` is set**: renders `EtText` with `data.subtitle`, `numberOfLines={1}`, and `ellipsizeMode` from context.
- **Has children**: renders a horizontal row wrapper for custom composition.

## Internal Architecture

### 1) Data normalization (`useDefaults`)

`useDefaults({ data, layout, ellipsizeMode, maxWidth })` resolves defaults and returns a memoized context value of type `EtUserDefaults`:

- `layout`: defaults to `'horizontal'`
- `ellipsizeMode`: defaults to `'tail'`
- `maxWidth`: passed through only when layout is horizontal; set to `undefined` in vertical layout
- `data`: spread from input; `data.avatar` is normalized when present

### 2) Child slot extraction (`useSlots`)

`useSlots(children)` scans children by `displayName` and extracts slots:

- `EtUserInfo.Avatar`
- `EtUserInfo.Title`
- `EtUserInfo.Subtitle`

### 3) Context boundary

`EtUserInfo` provides `EtUserInfoContext`, and subcomponents read it via `useEtUserInfoContext()`.

- Using subcomponents outside `EtUserInfo` throws runtime errors.

### 4) Layout rendering

- `horizontal`: renders `avatar` + text block (`title` + `subtitle`), with optional `maxWidth` style on text block.
- `vertical`: renders `avatar`, `title`, `subtitle` sequentially.
- Root container uses design-system spacing (`X2`, `X3`) and `alignSelf: 'flex-start'`.

## Usage Patterns

### Data-driven title and subtitle (empty slots)

```tsx
<EtUserInfo
  data={{
    avatar: {
      source: user.avatarUrl,
      size: 'medium',
      alt: user.name,
    },
    title: user.name,
    subtitle: `@${user.username}`,
  }}
  layout="horizontal"
>
  <EtUserInfo.Avatar />
  <EtUserInfo.Title />
  <EtUserInfo.Subtitle />
</EtUserInfo>
```

### Vertical user card

```tsx
<EtUserInfo
  data={{
    avatar: { source: user.avatarUrl, size: 'large' },
    title: user.name,
    subtitle: user.bio,
  }}
  layout="vertical"
>
  <EtUserInfo.Avatar />
  <EtUserInfo.Title />
  <EtUserInfo.Subtitle />
</EtUserInfo>
```

## Anti-patterns

### ❌ Using subcomponents outside root provider

```tsx
// BAD - throws at runtime
<EtUserInfo.Title>Jane Doe</EtUserInfo.Title>
```

Fix: Always render subcomponents inside `<EtUserInfo>...</EtUserInfo>`.

### ❌ Missing avatar source

```tsx
// BAD - EtUserInfo.Avatar renders null when source is missing or empty
<EtUserInfo data={{ title: 'Jane Doe' }}>
  <EtUserInfo.Avatar />
</EtUserInfo>
```

Fix: Provide `data.avatar.source` whenever an avatar is required.

